dialect protocol
protocol stdio.bcf.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.bcf
start entries
framing chunked

# FG-wave: `stdio.bcf` (bcfzip) is a PLAIN ZIP container -- deliberately NOT OPC (see this facet's
# text sibling, `../📝️text/📖️.grammar.semio`, for the full deviation-from-brief
# rationale, confirmed by direct read of `⚙️engine/🦀️.rs`'s own module doc comment). Its
# real codec (`encode_bcf`/`decode_bcf`, :397-414/416-473) delegates the ENTIRE byte-level
# container to `crate::artifacts::zip::engine::{encode_zip,decode_zip}` DIRECTLY -- one layer
# BELOW docx/xlsx/pptx's own `zip::opc::{encode_opc,decode_opc}` call, but the exact SAME real ZIP
# 2.0 byte layout underneath either way. So the byte layout THIS file must describe is, byte for
# byte, zip's own real ZIP 2.0 layout -- restated verbatim from
# `🎒️zip/🏅️standards/🔖️2.0/🪆️subsets/✳️markup/🧬️schema/📸️snapshot/💾️binary/📡️.protocol.semio`
# (the OPC-family citation precedent this ticket's brief names, ALSO the correct precedent for
# bcf's own non-OPC-but-still-real-zip container), identically to how
# `📜️docx/🏅️standards/🔖️ecma-376/…/📸️snapshot/💾️binary/📡️.protocol.semio` already restated
# it for the OPC case -- since cross-artifact `use` does not resolve at walk time
# (`📖️grammar-recipe.md` §2.1/§3), only `protocol`/`schema` differ from zip's own file; every
# field, tag, and M2 construct below is identical. Models the bytes as if the walk already starts
# AT the payload, past the SEMIO envelope (M3's own guidance, not re-described here).
#
# Three real structures, in this exact block order (each `arm 0x504B....` tag literal is the
# BIG-ENDIAN byte representation of the real on-disk 4-byte magic, e.g. `0x504B0304` decodes to
# bytes `50 4B 03 04` = literal `PK\x03\x04`):
#
# 1. `entries` (repeat, forward from byte 0): local file headers + per-entry payload
#    (`PK\x03\x04`) -- for bcf this is every real entry `encode_bcf` writes: `bcf.version`,
#    `<guid>/markup.bcf`, `<guid>/<guid>.bcfv`, `<guid>/<guid>.png` (the viewpoint snapshot image
#    bytes), and any raw-retained unmodeled part (`BcfRawPart`, e.g. `project.bcfp`) -- until the
#    first central-directory signature (`PK\x01\x02`) is seen.
# 2. `eocd` (backward-scan): ZIP's End Of Central Directory record is genuinely NOT locatable by a
#    forward walk (its own comment field is 0-65535 bytes) -- scans backward from EOF for
#    `PK\x05\x06`, same real necessity zip's own file documents.
# 3. `central_dir_start` (jump) + `central_directory` (repeat): `cd_offset`, decoded by the
#    backward-scan block above, is the ABSOLUTE offset of the first central-directory record --
#    `jump` repositions `pos` there (M2's cross-block field-env threading), then
#    `central_directory` reads the real, repeated per-entry metadata (`PK\x01\x02`) until the EOCD
#    signature (already fully captured by block 2) is seen again.
#
# Per M2's own report (`p2-m2-report.md`, deviation #1) and the plan's own explicit latitude: the
# OPTIONAL per-entry `local_off` backward-jump-to-local-header cross-validation `decode_zip` also
# performs is NOT modeled here -- `repeat`'s arm bodies cannot yet embed a `jump` sub-directive per
# iteration (M2's own documented boundary, `repeat-cannot-embed-jump` in
# `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §5) -- the central directory's own real per-entry fields (incl.
# `local_off` itself, decoded but not dereferenced) are the honest, complete model this wave ships.
#
# Also NOT modeled: the optional trailing streaming data-descriptor (general-purpose bit 3) after
# an entry's payload -- `encode_zip` NEVER emits one (always clears bit 3), matching zip's own
# file's identical carve-out.
#
# Because this file declares `backward`/`jump` blocks, the walk is (correctly, per M2's own
# documented exception) no longer required to land on exactly `bytes.len()`.

# ── 1. Local file headers + payload, forward from byte 0 ──────────────────────────────────────
repeat entries {
  tag fixed 4
  until 0x504B0102
  arm 0x504B0304 {
    version_needed u16
    flags u16
    method u16
    dos_time u16
    dos_date u16
    crc32 u32
    comp_size u32
    uncomp_size u32
    name_len u16
    extra_len u16
    name Array(u8, Field(name_len))
    extra Array(u8, Field(extra_len))
    payload Array(u8, Field(comp_size))
  }
  arm 0x504B0102 { }
}

# ── 2. EOCD, located by scanning backward from EOF for its own magic ──────────────────────────
backward eocd magic 0x504B0506 {
  disk_number u16
  disk_cd u16
  count u16
  total_count u16
  cd_size u32
  cd_offset u32
  comment_len u16
  comment Array(u8, Field(comment_len))
}

# ── 3. Jump to the central directory's first record, then walk it forward, repeated ───────────
jump central_dir_start from cd_offset { }

repeat central_directory {
  tag fixed 4
  until 0x504B0506
  arm 0x504B0102 {
    version_made_by u16
    version_needed u16
    flags u16
    method u16
    dos_time u16
    dos_date u16
    crc32 u32
    comp_size u32
    uncomp_size u32
    name_len u16
    extra_len u16
    comment_len u16
    disk_start u16
    internal_attrs u16
    external_attrs u32
    local_off u32
    name Array(u8, Field(name_len))
    extra Array(u8, Field(extra_len))
    comment Array(u8, Field(comment_len))
  }
  arm 0x504B0506 { }
}
